        "Name": "description_rich",
        "ValueType": "string",
        "StringValue": "Job Search RAG is a local LLM + retrieval pipeline modeled as a rulebook. Job boards get crawled, listings get normalized, the resume is chunked and embedded into ChromaDB, and every (listing, run) pair is scored on six dimensions — fit, archetype, history, comp, culture, negative — then fused into a single `FinalScore`. The interesting thing isn't the scraping; it's that every weight, every threshold, every rubric dimension lives in the rulebook as data. Change a `RubricDimension.SignalsNegative` row, and the next search run penalizes those phrases everywhere — across Postgres, Python, and the cosine-distance scorer — without touching a line of pipeline code.",
